  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is the best at 0.650 acc, and we know aggregation matters strongly for pca_n2000 (avgpool 0.591 >> transformer 0.519). Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the richer learned representations from scvi_n200 might interact differently with transformer aggregation than the linear pca_n2000 representations did. This experiment (config_006) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_005, isolating the aggregation choice while holding encoder (scvi_n200), profile (multiprofile), and modality (RNA) fixed. If transformer outperforms avgpool here, it opens a new optimization axis; if not, it confirms avgpool as the optimal aggregation for the best encoder, letting us allocate the remaining 3 experiments to testing whether multimodal fusion (with the best RNA backbone) can add incremental value over the 0.650 baseline."
}

